                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "08bffcee-2058-3072-a9c7-76e41b545dc6",
                        "entry_id": "a63c4535-4c8d-3ba7-9c1b-0b6b1d88da73",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Elements and interpretations of a fictional universe accepted by an individual or small group of fans, but not necessarily found within or supported by the official canon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "slang",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44e9358e-fe8e-4ef9-ab98-d11306f1628f",
                                "sense_id": "08bffcee-2058-3072-a9c7-76e41b545dc6",
                                "text": "In my own headcanon of Rocky IV, Ivan Drago is a Russian Mafia enforcer instead of a Red Army Captain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6fe39c4-02b5-4e8f-836d-15e6cd5a0b2e",
                                "sense_id": "08bffcee-2058-3072-a9c7-76e41b545dc6",
                                "text": "Technically, the social context of Borogravia is such that the actual external difference between a trans man and a woman disguised as a man is practically indiscernible – the technology level means they’re indistinguishable by the bodily modification standard (although now that I think about it, there's no reason Igors couldn't perform sex changes, and that's going in my headcanon now), and there does not appear to be a space in the language for self-identification."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d528f227-748a-42af-8392-46ce8a581887",
                                "sense_id": "08bffcee-2058-3072-a9c7-76e41b545dc6",
                                "text": "That wouldn't be so bad if it weren't for the fact that they just fill in the missing information with whatever headcanon (one's personal belief of what is true to the universe) they want instead of actually trying to find out more about the character."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a151aafc-475d-4096-b400-3c5a65de7444",
                                "sense_id": "08bffcee-2058-3072-a9c7-76e41b545dc6",
                                "text": "Don't forget if they can write pages and pages and pages of “headcanon” information for an already developed character, probably changing his or her already set personality or even expanding upon it."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
